        <detaileddescription>
<para><hruler/>
</para>
<para>2D steady-state calculation of parallel-plate permeability in a fracture set that is represented by a surface mesh. Subsequently, fluid pressure distribution is computed using a quadratic finite-element approximation. Dirichlet essential conditions are applied at left and right boundaries.</para>
<para>Later, the model is saved to a binary file and a new model is built from the vset file. The Dirichlet pressure boundary conditions are changed, the pressure is recomputed and the results are written to file</para>
<para>Use input mesh file set: veins_20k.1 as generated by program Triangle.</para>
<para>You can use either Paraview of the TCL/TK viewer &apos;example_viewer.tcl&apos; to visualize output.</para>
<para><xrefsect id="todo_1_todo000042"><xreftitle>Todo</xreftitle><xrefdescription><para>SKM: REWRITE: simplify the example to <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_v_set" kindref="compound">VSet</ref> operations: input and output only</para>
</xrefdescription></xrefsect></para>
        </detaileddescription>
